date-released: '2026-09-03'
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - interference
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - agent-based model
  - two-stage randomization
  - spillover effects
abstract: >-
  Self-contained R code reproducing every simulation result in
  "Advantages of a Two-Stage Randomized Trial Design to Evaluate
  Antimicrobial Treatment Strategies: a Simulation Study". A stochastic
  agent-based model of a hospital ward with two competing bacterial
  strains (drug-susceptible and drug-resistant) emulates a two-stage
  randomized trial: wards are randomized to a drug-allocation strategy
  and patients within a ward are randomized to a drug. The script
  estimates direct, indirect, total, and overall causal effects on
  mortality, along with the time-varying marginal direct effect, and
  reproduces all main-text and supplementary tables and figures from a
  single simulation run.
